2025-05-01 02:49:39 - Thread-1005 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Below are two parts:

PART 1 – Column “shopping‑list”: which columns look useful for each required attribute, together with typical filter ideas.  
PART 2 – Ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (all limited to 20 rows, all columns wrapped in double quotes, no casts except the illustrative ones for VARIANT columns).

────────────────────────
PART 1 – Relevant columns & possible conditions
────────────────────────
• "collection_id": will let us keep only TCGA‑LUAD / TCGA‑LUSC rows.  
    – Condition example: WHERE "collection_id" IN ('tcga_luad','tcga_lusc')  (values are lower‑case in IDC)

• "Modality": identifies slide‑microscopy images (‘SM’).  
    – Condition: WHERE "Modality" = 'SM'

• "ImageType" and/or "FrameType": both are VARIANT arrays that usually contain the keyword VOLUME for whole‑slide images.  
    – Condition: ("ImageType" ILIKE '%VOLUME%' OR "FrameType" ILIKE '%VOLUME%')

• Compression information  
  – "TransferSyntaxUID":  
        1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.50 = JPEG baseline  
        1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70 = JPEG lossless  
        1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.90 = JPEG‑LS  
        1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.91 = JPEG‑LS lossless  
        1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.95 = JPEG‑2000  
  – We may label everything else as “other”.  
    – Condition: "TransferSyntaxUID" IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.50','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.90','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.91','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.95')

• “SpecimenDescriptionSequence” (VARIANT) → contains nested content items such as (0040,0554) Specimen Preparation Step Content Item Seq.  
    – We need to locate content items whose (0040,A043) “Concept Name Code Sequence” has code 430864009 (“Embedding medium”) **and** where the related “Concept Code Sequence” has code 430858009 (“Tissue freezing medium”).  
    – Filter will therefore require a VARIANT search.

• Tissue type (normal / tumor)  
    – Usually stored in “SpecimenDescriptionSequence” inside Content Items whose concept name is “Morphology” (118171006) or “Histologic type” etc.  
    – Codes of interest:  
         17621005  → normal tissue  
         86049000  → tumor tissue  
    – We can label them via CASE.

• Digital‑slide ID  
    – Often equals "SeriesInstanceUID" (all WSI tiles reside in one series).  
    – Alternative is “InstanceNumber”; in TCGA WSI there is exactly one instance per series, so "SOPInstanceUID" is unique for the digital slide as well.  
    – In practice most people use "SOPInstanceUID" as the unique slide identifier.

• Case ID / Patient ID  
    – "idc_case_id" → IDC case (i.e. subject) UUID.  
    – "PatientID"   → TCGA barcode without the final slice designation.

• Physical slide ID  
    – "ContainerIdentifier" (0018,1007) usually stores the barcode of the glass slide.

• Width / Height  
    – "Columns", "Rows".

• Pixel spacing  
    – "ImagerPixelSpacing" (0028,0030) or, if missing, "PixelSpacing" (0028,0030).

• Instance ID  
    – "SOPInstanceUID"

• GCS path  
    – "gcs_url"

────────────────────────
PART 2 – 10 exploratory SQL snippets
────────────────────────
```sql
-- 1. Quick peek at all collections that contain SM images
SELECT DISTINCT "collection_id"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE "Modality" = 'SM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Verify the exact spelling of LUAD / LUSC collections
SELECT DISTINCT "collection_id"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE "collection_id" ILIKE '%tcga%lu%'
  AND "Modality" = 'SM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. How many SM rows for each of the two collections?
SELECT "collection_id",
       COUNT(*) AS "num_sm_instances"
FROM   "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE  "collection_id" IN ('tcga_luad','tcga_lusc')
  AND  "Modality" = 'SM'
GROUP BY "collection_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Inspect ImageType / FrameType strings to see how 'VOLUME' appears
SELECT "SOPInstanceUID",
       "ImageType",
       "FrameType"
FROM   "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE  "collection_id" IN ('tcga_luad','tcga_lusc')
  AND  "Modality" = 'SM'
  AND  ("ImageType" ILIKE '%VOLUME%' OR "FrameType" ILIKE '%VOLUME%')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Distinct transfer syntaxes used by SM slides in the two target collections
SELECT DISTINCT "TransferSyntaxUID"
FROM   "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE  "collection_id" IN ('tcga_luad','tcga_lusc')
  AND  "Modality" = 'SM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Check rows whose SpecimenDescriptionSequence mentions 'Tissue freezing medium'
SELECT d."SOPInstanceUID",
       f.value AS "specimen_item"
FROM   "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"  d,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => d."SpecimenDescriptionSequence") f
WHERE  d."collection_id" IN ('tcga_luad','tcga_lusc')
  AND  d."Modality" = 'SM'
  AND  f.value::STRING ILIKE '%freezing%medium%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Same flatten technique, but now inspect any embedded SNOMED codes (17621005 / 86049000)
SELECT d."SOPInstanceUID",
       f.value AS "specimen_item"
FROM   "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"  d,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => d."SpecimenDescriptionSequence") f
WHERE  d."collection_id" IN ('tcga_luad','tcga_lusc')
  AND  d."Modality" = 'SM'
  AND ( f.value::STRING ILIKE '%17621005%'  -- normal
     OR f.value::STRING ILIKE '%86049000%'  -- tumor
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Look at coordinates + pixel spacing for a few candidate slides
SELECT "SOPInstanceUID",
       "Rows",
       "Columns",
       COALESCE("ImagerPixelSpacing","PixelSpacing") AS "px_spacing",
       "TransferSyntaxUID"
FROM   "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE  "collection_id" IN ('tcga_luad','tcga_lusc')
  AND  "Modality" = 'SM'
  AND  ("ImageType" ILIKE '%VOLUME%' OR "FrameType" ILIKE '%VOLUME%')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Pull core metadata including ContainerIdentifier (physical slide bar‑code)
SELECT "SOPInstanceUID",
       "SeriesInstanceUID",
       "ContainerIdentifier",
       "PatientID",
       "idc_case_id",
       "gcs_url"
FROM   "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE  "collection_id" IN ('tcga_luad','tcga_lusc')
  AND  "Modality" = 'SM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Attempt an integrated view that already narrows by most key constraints
SELECT
       d."SOPInstanceUID"                      AS "instance_id",
       d."SeriesInstanceUID"                   AS "digital_slide_id",
       d."ContainerIdentifier"                 AS "physical_slide_id",
       d."PatientID"                           AS "patient_id",
       d."idc_case_id"                         AS "case_id",
       d."collection_id",
       d."gcs_url",
       d."Rows"                                AS "height_px",
       d."Columns"                             AS "width_px",
       COALESCE(d."ImagerPixelSpacing",d."PixelSpacing") AS "pixel_spacing",
       d."TransferSyntaxUID"
FROM   "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL" d
WHERE  d."collection_id" IN ('tcga_luad','tcga_lusc')
  AND  d."Modality"      = 'SM'
  AND  (d."ImageType" ILIKE '%VOLUME%' OR d."FrameType" ILIKE '%VOLUME%')
  AND  d."TransferSyntaxUID" IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.50',  -- JPEG
                                 '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70',
                                 '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.90',
                                 '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.91',
                                 '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.95')   -- JPEG2000
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM   LATERAL FLATTEN(input => d."SpecimenDescriptionSequence") s
        WHERE  s.value::STRING ILIKE '%freezing%medium%'
      )
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM   LATERAL FLATTEN(input => d."SpecimenDescriptionSequence") t
        WHERE  t.value::STRING ILIKE '%17621005%'  -- normal
           OR  t.value::STRING ILIKE '%86049000%'  -- tumor
      )
LIMIT 20;
```
The ten snippets progress from simple inspections (collections, modality) through nested VARIANT exploration, culminating in a near‑final integrated query (still limited to 20 rows for interactive examination).
